# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_ingest_overcap.py" "INGEST OVERCAP GATE: PASS" "ingest cost-guard counts what build_graph actually ingests (not every file)" "ingest over-cap: the _full_ingest cost guard probes the file count with the EXACT pruning build_graph uses (reuses code_graph_extract._iter_source_files/_iter_config_files -> same _SKIP_DIRS / _is_generated / _SOURCE_EXT,_CONFIG_EXTS allowlists, no divergent copy), so a repo of ~100 real code files + ~12,900 vendored/doc/image files (bloat build_graph SKIPS) PASSES the cap and is INGESTED (a non-empty graph -> the public meter reads real coverage) instead of being stored as an EMPTY graph + read as 0 files (the silent-miss + billing defect); the count EQUALS the file-node count build_graph emits (cannot drift); a vendored/skip-dir/doc-only tree counts ZERO; and the DoS guard is PRESERVED -- a repo with > _MAX_INGEST_FILES REAL code files still trips the cap (empty graph, honest 'unknown', never OOM). OFFLINE (temp dir + in-memory tarball + recording fake db/gh, no Postgres), content-free, never-crash" "ingest over-cap: the cost guard counts ONLY what build_graph ingests (reusing the extractor's own skip predicates) -> vendored/doc bloat no longer trips the cap (empty graph -> 0-file silent miss + free-tier billing leak); count == build_graph's file nodes (no drift); DoS guard preserved for > cap REAL code files" 24
